# Canvas downloads. Student work must never be committed: these folders carry
# real names and real writing, and this repo is public because GitHub Pages
# serves it.
submissions/
submissions.zip
*_submissions/
responses.csv
exceptions.csv

# The assessment bank and everything generated from it.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC, because GitHub Pages serves it, and .nojekyll means
# every committed file is served verbatim at a guessable URL. An exam committed
# here is a published exam, an answer key committed here is a published answer
# key, and git history keeps both after a delete. Unlike a wrong link or a stale
# target, that one cannot be repaired by fixing it: the moment a student has read
# the questions, the assessment is spent.
#
# So the generator, its gate, and the README are in the repo, and the questions
# and answers are not. docs/assessments/README.md says where they do live.
#
# The -KEY line is deliberately redundant with the blanket line above it. If
# somebody ever un-ignores this folder to commit a blank practice sheet, the
# files carrying answers stay ignored anyway, and validate.js checks that this
# pattern exists.
scripts/lib/assessment-content/
docs/assessments/*
!docs/assessments/README.md
docs/assessments/*-KEY*
